            {
                "entry_id": "22e70bbf-4d2f-33c1-a8eb-b06ad3ed5ab3",
                "word": "Belter",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "63154adb-4826-49f7-a00a-27df599c0e96",
                        "entry_id": "22e70bbf-4d2f-33c1-a8eb-b06ad3ed5ab3",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "Belters"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "03a13411-28ad-3016-b9e1-9146104b59b2",
                        "entry_id": "22e70bbf-4d2f-33c1-a8eb-b06ad3ed5ab3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An inhabitant of an asteroid belt, especially that between Mars and Jupiter."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "64b08678-67d7-403e-a4df-a32094b09c7d",
                                "sense_id": "03a13411-28ad-3016-b9e1-9146104b59b2",
                                "text": "You noticed a habit of mine once. I never make gestures. All Belters have that trait. It's because on a small mining ship you could hit something waving your arms around."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3e8fde55-fa8f-4530-81bb-accb96bc5159",
                                "sense_id": "03a13411-28ad-3016-b9e1-9146104b59b2",
                                "text": "Earth and Mars have been stepping on the necks of the Belters out here for over 100 years and I didn't want to be the boot."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cb4bc66c-5b8b-4569-8208-1780207d7029",
                                "sense_id": "03a13411-28ad-3016-b9e1-9146104b59b2",
                                "text": "He also decided that Belters wouldn’t use the term “bullshit,” because there would be no bulls in the Belt. Instead, they would come up with a uniquely Belter curse, “kaka felota,” a term for what happens when your toilet backs up in low gravity and shit floats all over the place. (“Kata felota” literally means “floating shit.”)"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
